@@ -8,6 +8,18 @@ package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.
 
 ## [Unreleased]
 
+### Changed
+
+- `ToolRegistry` now compiles static `ToolDefinition.inputSchema` values with `ajv` at
+  registration time (throwing an error naming the tool on invalid schemas), caches compiled
+  validators for function-valued tool definitions by schema object reference, and validates
+  `ToolRegistry.execute` inputs against the resolved schema before calling the executor,
+  returning a `ToolResponse` naming failing fields and constraints on rejection without echoing
+  or logging offending property values. Executors now receive only inputs accepted by
+  `inputSchema` (`required`, declared types, and `enum`), with undeclared extra properties
+  passed through unchanged without coercion or defaults, so tools that previously relied on
+  seeing malformed input to emit their own error messages will no longer receive it.
+
